# Normalize line endings on checkout everywhere.
#
# Without this, Windows checks text files out with CRLF, which changes their
# bytes. That silently broke the claims registry: fixture hashes are content
# hashes, so the same fixture produced a different digest on Windows and every
# registered claim failed as "stale". validate-claims also normalizes before
# hashing, but pinning the checkout keeps the two from ever disagreeing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.tgz binary
*.db binary
